Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The Lie algebra of classical mechanics", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"62afe9f6-8cb7-4c76-ae35-c2a944153ee2"],

Cell["\<\
The Lie algebra of classical mechanics is the quotient L(A,B)/I of the free \
Lie algebra by the Lie ideal I generated by [B,[B,[B,A]]]. It models the Lie \
algebra generated, under the Poisson bracket, by a kinetic energy A, \
quadratic in the momenta, and a potential energy B. See R. I. McLachlan and \
A. Murua, The Lie algebra of classical mechanics, J. Comput. Dyn. 6 (2019) \
345-360, https://doi.org/10.3934/jcd.2019017, arXiv:1905.07554.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"26fe7077-e988-47da-bfed-fb923e665d36"],

Cell["\<\
To work in L(A,B)/I, initialize with LieAlgebra -> \"ClassicalMechanics\". \
Lie series are still computed as elements of L(A,B), but their coefficients \
and their display refer to L(A,B)/I:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f530e726-f804-464c-ae99-4f5ffc03d9e6"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
LieSeriesInitialize[{\"A\", \"B\"}, 6, LieAlgebra -> \"ClassicalMechanics\"];
A = LieSeries[\"A\"]; B = LieSeries[\"B\"];
HallBasisElements[5]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[58]:=",ExpressionUUID->"c0583f28-08eb-47b6-a091-1485bb84a4bd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"A\"\>", ",", "\<\"B\"\>", ",", 
